WEBVTT

00:03.980 --> 00:05.610
Roger!

00:08.570 --> 00:09.360
Hurry!

00:11.990 --> 00:13.660
Ram 'em!

00:18.160 --> 00:19.750
Hang on tight!

00:54.530 --> 00:56.950
Are you the captain of the Bardanos?

01:07.630 --> 01:07.670
LEIJI MATSUMOTO'S

01:07.630 --> 01:07.670
OZMA

01:13.640 --> 01:16.600
You looked over the desert wasteland from above

01:16.600 --> 01:19.810
kareki wo sora de mioroshita

01:16.600 --> 01:19.810
and saw dead trees scattered throughout

01:19.810 --> 01:25.480
aoi tori ga nageki naku to

01:19.810 --> 01:25.480
Blue bird, who knows no sadness

01:26.070 --> 01:28.990
machigai darake no kibou no

01:26.070 --> 01:28.990
I ground my teeth, my hope full of misconceptions

01:28.990 --> 01:33.950
okuba de kanda nigai suna hakidasenai

01:28.990 --> 01:33.950
and couldn't spit out the dreadful sand in my mouth

01:33.950 --> 01:39.080
atoaji wa namida he to toketa

01:33.950 --> 01:39.080
Left was only the salt of tears

01:39.080 --> 01:44.500
aisuru mono sae mamorenai okubyou mono ni

01:39.080 --> 01:44.500
For cowards unable to protect the ones they love

01:44.500 --> 01:50.260
michitarita asa wa konai

01:44.500 --> 01:50.260
no future waits past the dawn of day

01:50.630 --> 01:51.420
Woah

01:51.010 --> 01:51.760
oh

01:51.420 --> 01:52.260
oh!

01:51.800 --> 01:56.720
asu no tobira doko he tsuzuitemo

01:51.800 --> 01:56.720
Wherever the door to the future may lead

01:56.720 --> 02:01.930
haruka misueta me wa nidoto sorasanai

01:56.720 --> 02:01.930
I'll stay focused on what I need to do for it myself

02:01.930 --> 02:03.390
Oh,

02:03.020 --> 02:03.810
woah

02:03.350 --> 02:04.270
oh

02:03.810 --> 02:04.600
oh!

02:04.190 --> 02:08.980
itoshiki kimi no kokoro tataku yo

02:04.190 --> 02:08.980
I will take my place in your heart

02:08.980 --> 02:18.240
itsuka tadashii sekai he kimi wo tsureteyuku kara

02:08.980 --> 02:18.240
because one day I will show you the world we should live in

02:32.420 --> 02:37.390
Episode 5: The Masked Man

02:38.390 --> 02:41.770
I am Gido Gailar,
commander of the Theseus Fleet.

02:43.430 --> 02:44.770
Bainas.

02:45.400 --> 02:47.440
That was a splendid battle.

02:48.020 --> 02:51.530
I wanted to meet my enemy face-to-face.

02:51.530 --> 02:53.030
As did I.

02:53.950 --> 02:55.410
Why do you pursue us?

02:56.320 --> 02:58.700
We want Maya back.

02:58.700 --> 03:03.960
Unfortunately, I'm not able
to abandon people in need.

03:04.710 --> 03:05.790
I refuse.

03:07.500 --> 03:11.630
Miss Maya is an important person to us.

03:14.510 --> 03:16.930
Then I'll take her by force!

03:31.320 --> 03:32.820
Captain!

03:32.820 --> 03:36.320
We're being approached by
something with a massive QTF!

03:37.200 --> 03:37.780
Ozma?

03:38.030 --> 03:38.990
What?

03:43.580 --> 03:44.500
Ozma!

03:51.000 --> 03:53.130
We'll settle things next time!

03:54.510 --> 03:56.010
After all this time, it's here!

03:56.340 --> 03:58.090
It's finally here!

03:58.090 --> 03:59.430
Prepare to dive!

03:59.640 --> 04:00.800
What?

04:01.430 --> 04:04.350
Damn it! Everything's still rattled
from that last shock!

04:07.640 --> 04:08.600
What is this?

04:08.600 --> 04:10.900
It's Ozma. That's his roar!

04:17.280 --> 04:18.650
Dive, now!

04:33.420 --> 04:34.960
Damage report, now!

04:34.960 --> 04:36.420
Propeller shaft damaged!

04:36.420 --> 04:37.470
We can't steer!

05:27.640 --> 05:29.890
Wh-Where are we?

05:31.020 --> 05:32.600
C-Captain?

05:32.600 --> 05:34.020
Confirm our position!

05:34.020 --> 05:36.570
I want to know exactly
what's going on outside the ship.

05:36.570 --> 05:37.440
Roger!

05:37.440 --> 05:38.900
Get yer asses movin'!

05:39.360 --> 05:41.320
Inspect those engines!

05:41.320 --> 05:45.200
Don't miss a single crack!

05:45.200 --> 05:46.030
Roger!

05:46.450 --> 05:47.910
This is the engine room.

05:47.910 --> 05:51.410
Gimme 'bout an hour
till we can start movin' again.

05:51.410 --> 05:52.330
Roger.

05:52.710 --> 05:54.330
Oh, my.

05:55.540 --> 05:58.750
Looks like it'll be a busy day for us, Mickey.

06:02.930 --> 06:04.930
Torpedo launch room, all clear.

06:05.340 --> 06:07.890
What the hell's goin' on here?

06:08.180 --> 06:09.560
What happened?

06:10.060 --> 06:12.020
The main monitor's down.

06:12.690 --> 06:14.980
But the sensors are working.

06:14.980 --> 06:17.360
Hull pressure zero?
We're in an open space!

06:17.860 --> 06:20.940
Atmosphere composition: 73%.

06:20.940 --> 06:23.070
Oxygen: 25.9%.

06:23.070 --> 06:25.360
Carbon dioxide: 0.04%.

06:26.320 --> 06:28.780
So we can breathe out there?

06:28.780 --> 06:30.040
Easily.

06:30.040 --> 06:32.040
It looks like there's fresh water, too.

06:32.040 --> 06:35.370
But... where exactly are we?

06:35.370 --> 06:36.130
Leave it to me!

06:36.420 --> 06:37.790
I'll go check it out!

06:37.790 --> 06:38.590
Sam!

06:38.590 --> 06:40.760
There's air and water.

06:40.760 --> 06:43.340
So why don't we go see for ourselves?

06:43.340 --> 06:45.180
That'll be my job!

06:45.380 --> 06:46.430
I'll go, too.

06:47.220 --> 06:48.720
What're you gonna do?

06:48.720 --> 06:49.810
You'll just get in the wa-

06:58.650 --> 07:00.650
Don't blame me if anything happens.

07:02.150 --> 07:03.530
Look out!

07:06.110 --> 07:08.030
Hey, watch where you're going!

07:08.030 --> 07:09.080
Shut up.

07:09.080 --> 07:11.540
You wouldn't last a second on your own!

07:15.120 --> 07:16.420
What is this?

07:16.420 --> 07:18.540
Wow!

07:26.720 --> 07:29.470
I can't believe
there's a lake like this underground.

07:29.470 --> 07:32.390
I've never seen one this big.

07:37.850 --> 07:41.230
This is so different from the
desert world we've always known.

07:41.820 --> 07:43.990
There're all kinds of living things down here.

07:43.990 --> 07:45.740
Could there be people as well?

07:45.740 --> 07:47.820
That's what we're here to find out!

07:53.870 --> 07:55.040
That's...

07:55.410 --> 07:57.330
Theseus's ship?

07:57.790 --> 07:59.750
Looks like they ended up here, too.

08:09.220 --> 08:10.430
Sam!

08:10.430 --> 08:12.100
Stay away from that thing!
It's not safe!

08:12.100 --> 08:14.350
We should go back and report to the captain!

08:22.860 --> 08:24.360
What do you think you're doing?

08:24.360 --> 08:25.740
What else?

08:25.740 --> 08:27.400
I'm gonna save Maya.

08:27.400 --> 08:30.280
Don't! We need to talk to the captain first!

08:30.280 --> 08:31.200
Do what you want.

08:31.740 --> 08:33.620
You saw how frail Maya is.

08:33.620 --> 08:36.000
We can't wait any longer!

08:39.250 --> 08:40.330
Sam!

08:40.330 --> 08:41.460
Don't worry!

08:41.830 --> 08:43.000
I won't do anything crazy.

08:44.170 --> 08:46.760
Jeez, you never listen.

08:47.260 --> 08:48.840
I'll call the captain!

08:48.840 --> 08:50.260
I'll be waiting!

08:51.050 --> 08:52.640
Hang in there, Maya.

08:53.220 --> 08:55.010
I'm coming for you!

09:39.980 --> 09:41.560
How is Miss Maya?

09:41.560 --> 09:42.900
She's fine.

09:42.900 --> 09:44.940
What about the ship?

09:44.940 --> 09:46.900
The engineers are looking at it.

09:47.320 --> 09:48.650
Over there?

09:54.530 --> 09:56.660
Oh, crap...

09:57.790 --> 09:59.750
We found the Theseus ship!

10:00.040 --> 10:02.580
Sam just boarded it on his own...

10:02.580 --> 10:04.830
What's wrong, everyone?

10:06.250 --> 10:08.710
We just got a message from Theseus.

10:09.590 --> 10:11.760
They've taken Sam as a hostage.

10:12.590 --> 10:13.630
That idiot...

10:13.630 --> 10:17.510
"If you want him back,
send the captain herself," they said.

10:18.140 --> 10:19.220
How are the repairs?

10:20.220 --> 10:21.930
Monitors are back online.

10:22.140 --> 10:25.150
Can we get close to the
Theseus ship over the water?

10:25.860 --> 10:27.310
Yes, I think so.

10:27.310 --> 10:29.110
Okay. Let's move!

10:29.110 --> 10:29.980
Roger!

10:31.320 --> 10:33.200
Damn it! Let me go!

10:33.990 --> 10:35.320
You bastard!

10:35.570 --> 10:37.030
You better not have hurt Maya!

10:37.030 --> 10:37.910
Silence!

10:41.370 --> 10:42.750
Stay put.

10:46.330 --> 10:47.380
Bardanos!

10:49.000 --> 10:49.960
Captain!

10:51.260 --> 10:52.130
So she came.

10:52.130 --> 10:53.630
Captain, I'm sorry!

10:54.800 --> 10:55.800
Gido.

10:55.800 --> 10:57.390
Looks like you're stuck.

10:58.300 --> 11:02.140
You got trapped before
you could escape the QTF, huh?

11:03.390 --> 11:06.020
You don't have time
for this right now, do you?

11:06.480 --> 11:08.520
If you want to get out of here,
I'll help you.

11:09.730 --> 11:12.320
In your position,
you think you can tell <i>us</i> what to do?

11:14.650 --> 11:17.160
Hand over your ship.

11:22.660 --> 11:23.540
Bainas.

11:25.460 --> 11:29.130
Do you know what this place,
the Zone, is?

11:29.840 --> 11:32.340
No. You have no idea.

11:32.880 --> 11:34.630
This is a seed bank.

11:36.380 --> 11:39.970
You could call it a laboratory
for the evolution of life.

11:41.220 --> 11:45.100
Together, Maya and I can rule this land.

11:46.060 --> 11:49.440
We can control all life on this planet!

11:50.110 --> 11:52.610
All who bow to us will live,

11:52.610 --> 11:54.740
and all who oppose us will die.

11:55.610 --> 11:59.990
We will create a beautiful world,
with me at its apex!

12:02.200 --> 12:06.080
I thought you would be easier to talk to.

12:06.080 --> 12:10.540
But from what I'm hearing,
you're no different to that idiot general.

12:10.540 --> 12:12.290
What did you say?

12:12.290 --> 12:14.000
Stop it, Gido.

12:16.340 --> 12:18.930
Maya? You're safe?

12:18.930 --> 12:20.720
Put down your weapon.

12:21.260 --> 12:25.600
I will not allow needless conflict
in this land of hope.

12:26.560 --> 12:29.020
Please return to the ship, Miss Maya.

12:29.770 --> 12:32.610
We will have need for your power soon,

12:32.610 --> 12:34.940
but now is not the time.

12:35.650 --> 12:37.070
Now, Bainas.

12:37.650 --> 12:39.990
Order your men off the ship,

12:39.990 --> 12:42.070
and hand over the Bardanos.

12:42.320 --> 12:43.410
If you don't...

12:46.250 --> 12:47.330
Gido!

12:51.710 --> 12:52.540
Damn it!

12:53.460 --> 12:53.960
Guys!

12:53.960 --> 12:54.710
This way, Sam!

13:00.880 --> 13:02.430
Damn it!

13:09.350 --> 13:10.390
You okay?

13:10.390 --> 13:11.190
Mimay!

13:39.970 --> 13:40.670
Did you see that?

13:40.670 --> 13:41.800
Yes.

13:41.800 --> 13:42.720
I'm sure of it.

13:43.340 --> 13:46.600
That was my brother Dick.

13:48.520 --> 13:49.850
Maya!

13:50.100 --> 13:51.140
Wait for me.

13:51.140 --> 13:52.560
I'll come back.

13:53.940 --> 13:55.020
Sam!

14:07.870 --> 14:11.910
Captain Gido went missing
after telling us he was on his way back.

14:15.250 --> 14:18.090
I can't believe he disappeared with Miss Maya.

14:18.090 --> 14:21.260
Does he have that little pride?

14:22.420 --> 14:27.350
He's a fool, entranced by petty desires.

14:28.180 --> 14:30.720
Mobilize the whole army!

14:40.980 --> 14:43.740
Dick, was that really you?

14:48.240 --> 14:49.240
Sam...

14:50.910 --> 14:52.200
Captain!

14:52.200 --> 14:54.080
Well? Did you find him?

14:54.080 --> 14:55.120
Well...

14:56.670 --> 14:57.630
This is...

14:58.750 --> 15:00.300
Gido's mask?

15:00.300 --> 15:02.380
You saw it, Captain.

15:02.380 --> 15:03.880
That was him!

15:03.880 --> 15:05.550
It wasn't Gido!

15:06.840 --> 15:09.140
It was... Dick.

15:09.970 --> 15:11.560
My brother.

15:13.180 --> 15:14.270
That can't...

15:14.810 --> 15:16.270
That can't be...

15:26.780 --> 15:29.200
C'mon, take it like a man! Pipe down!

15:45.420 --> 15:46.260
Sam...

15:47.130 --> 15:53.720
I wanted to follow in my
brother's footsteps by defeating Ozma.

15:53.720 --> 15:58.600
Or, really... I thought that,
if I defeated Ozma,

15:58.600 --> 16:04.230
my brother would come back to me somehow.

16:05.360 --> 16:06.740
Sam...

16:07.200 --> 16:12.740
That he'd smile and say,
"Sam, you've gotten strong."

16:13.870 --> 16:16.500
I knew it was stupid,
but I thought it anyway.

16:19.120 --> 16:21.750
But... But...

16:32.100 --> 16:32.970
Why?

16:33.600 --> 16:35.020
How?

16:37.770 --> 16:40.350
How did Dick turn into Gido Gailar?

16:40.350 --> 16:41.810
There's something I noticed.

16:42.860 --> 16:43.730
Doctor?

16:44.650 --> 16:47.240
Something strange that I noticed
while I was treating those soldiers.

16:49.240 --> 16:57.450
The bio-signs of those soldiers were closer
to us Natura than the Ideal Children.

16:58.210 --> 17:00.000
How could that be possible?

17:03.210 --> 17:04.210
Maya!

17:04.800 --> 17:08.970
Our ancestors,
the humans from ancient times,

17:08.970 --> 17:13.720
created the Ideal Children
using ideal genetic information.

17:17.270 --> 17:18.390
But...

17:18.390 --> 17:20.600
As they were cloned time and time again...

17:20.600 --> 17:27.730
The bodies and minds of the Ideal Children
have weakened over the generations.

17:30.240 --> 17:31.950
They realized...

17:32.610 --> 17:36.620
that as they gradually weakened,

17:36.620 --> 17:42.460
the Natura, while few in number,
were better able to adapt to the harsh environment,

17:42.460 --> 17:45.790
due to their natural reproduction.

17:47.710 --> 17:50.800
Some of the Ideal Children...

17:51.630 --> 17:58.350
decided to capture Natura and
implant their own minds into them.

18:00.350 --> 18:01.980
So strong...

18:09.110 --> 18:14.160
You mean... their bodies once belonged
to our companions?

18:16.200 --> 18:17.120
Yes.

18:17.120 --> 18:21.580
So they killed Dick's mind and took his body?

18:22.120 --> 18:23.420
That's right.

18:23.420 --> 18:24.920
You didn't stop them?!

18:24.920 --> 18:27.250
You're the queen of Theseus!

18:28.000 --> 18:31.880
There's nothing I can say
without it sounding like an excuse.

18:36.470 --> 18:42.270
Maya, when I treated you,
I also looked at your genetic information.

18:43.100 --> 18:46.360
You're not one of the Ideal Children either, are you?

18:50.780 --> 18:55.570
I am one of the humans from
ancient times, known as the Originals.

18:57.740 --> 19:06.500
I have lived this long by cloning myself
and moving my mind into each new body.

19:10.210 --> 19:14.220
Y-You mean, you've lived for centuries?

19:15.430 --> 19:19.260
That's why your telomeres are so short...

19:20.510 --> 19:22.520
I won't last much longer.

19:24.100 --> 19:29.440
That's why I have to come to a
decision before this body falls apart.

19:29.900 --> 19:32.030
That's why you've come here?

19:33.400 --> 19:37.360
Gido said this place was a lab for living things.

19:37.360 --> 19:40.240
Maya, what is hidden here?

19:41.280 --> 19:43.500
I have to choose.

19:43.950 --> 19:47.330
And for that, I have to meet Ozma.

19:47.500 --> 19:49.080
Ozma?

19:50.840 --> 19:51.880
Captain!

19:51.880 --> 19:54.130
We're hearing lots of engine sounds getting closer!

20:02.850 --> 20:05.930
The sensors are reading unusual EM waves.

20:05.930 --> 20:06.890
They're close.

20:08.020 --> 20:10.650
To protect our honor,

20:10.650 --> 20:16.740
we must be prepared to
choose a hopeless future.

20:21.990 --> 20:23.120
What's wrong?

20:23.120 --> 20:24.410
That's Ozma's voice!

20:25.660 --> 20:26.500
What's wrong?

20:28.460 --> 20:29.620
Maya!

20:29.620 --> 20:31.040
I can hear it...

20:31.040 --> 20:34.300
But this voice...
I've never heard it before.

20:34.300 --> 20:36.590
What can you hear?

20:36.590 --> 20:39.550
Ozma... Ozma is angry!

20:39.550 --> 20:40.800
What?

20:40.800 --> 20:42.300
Captain!

20:42.850 --> 20:44.970
Ozma! Ozma is coming!

20:51.520 --> 20:52.860
Ozma!

20:57.860 --> 20:58.990
It's huge!

20:59.200 --> 21:01.240
It's going to swallow us!

21:09.040 --> 21:10.120
The Monokeros!

21:11.250 --> 21:12.080
Captain!

21:12.080 --> 21:13.130
Use the Monokeros!

21:13.420 --> 21:15.000
The weapon my brother left us!

21:15.000 --> 21:16.000
Sam!

21:19.260 --> 21:20.260
Captain!

21:24.390 --> 21:25.680
All crew to battle stations!

21:25.680 --> 21:27.020
We will engage the Ozma!

21:27.020 --> 21:29.230
Prepare to fire the Monokeros!

21:30.020 --> 21:36.530
shin'ai naru anata he

21:30.020 --> 21:36.530
I ask you, my love,

21:36.530 --> 21:43.910
since when your heart

21:42.910 --> 21:49.500
setsunasa to kodoku no aida

21:42.910 --> 21:49.500
has been lost between sorrow and solitude

21:49.500 --> 21:56.000
hasamarete kokyuu wo wasureteru

21:49.500 --> 21:56.000
where you lost your grip on reality

21:56.000 --> 22:02.510
kanashii uta ni tsutsumarete

21:56.000 --> 22:02.510
All around us we hear songs of lament

22:02.510 --> 22:09.020
namida ga ochiru sono mae ni

22:02.510 --> 22:09.020
but before I give in to the tears

22:08.010 --> 22:14.650
kizuite anata wo omoinagara

22:08.010 --> 22:14.650
I notice the echoes

22:14.650 --> 22:23.610
yasashiku hibiku utagoe ni

22:14.650 --> 22:23.610
of a gentle singing voice around me

22:23.860 --> 22:31.540
dareka wo aishite dareka ni aisare

22:23.860 --> 22:31.540
Loving someone and being loved by someone

22:30.540 --> 22:36.880
umareta imi ni sotto kizuketa nara

22:30.540 --> 22:36.880
is why we were all born

22:36.880 --> 22:44.380
omoi no mama ni koe wo furishibotte

22:36.880 --> 22:43.170
If you realized that too, put your emotions

22:42.170 --> 22:44.380
into your voice

22:44.380 --> 22:54.520
anata mo tsuyoku ai wo utatte hoshii

22:44.380 --> 22:54.520
and please sing of love with all your strength

22:59.940 --> 23:11.950
Next Episode

23:00.980 --> 23:02.360
The Ozma is heading straight for us!

23:02.360 --> 23:04.820
Who pissed off the sand whale?

23:04.820 --> 23:06.110
Fire the Monokeros!

23:06.110 --> 23:09.660
Wait! Sam and Mimay
are heading there with Maya!

23:09.660 --> 23:10.950
Please, Sam!

23:10.950 --> 23:14.000
Save the Bardanos!
Save this planet!

23:11.950 --> 23:14.960
Final Episode: The Day of New Life
